<% content_for :page_title, 'Directory & access' %><%= stylesheet_link_tag '/lightek/people-workspace.css' %><main class="lp-workspace"><header class="lp-heading"><div><span class="lp-eyebrow">LIGHTEK / IDENTITY</span><h1>Directory & access</h1><p>Connect organization sign-in, join remote servers to a domain and assign access by department or person.</p></div><%= link_to 'My sign-in security', identity_security_path, class: 'lp-button secondary' %></header><%= form_with url: dashboard_directory_path, method: :get, class: 'lp-form' do |f| %><label>Employer<%= select_tag :employer_id, options_from_collection_for_select(@employers,:id,:email_address,@employer.id) %></label><%= f.submit 'Switch employer', class: 'lp-button secondary' %><% end %>
<section class="lp-card"><h2>Accessible resources</h2><p>Read and manage are separate permissions. Server login does not grant sudo or access to accounting. Resource ownership and active employment are checked on each request.</p><div class="lp-departments"><% @nodes.each do |node| %><article><h3><%= node.name %></h3><p>Server · <%= node.status %></p><%= link_to 'Open server', dashboard_server_path(node), class: 'lp-button secondary' %></article><% end %><% @applications.each do |app| %><article><h3><%= app.name %></h3><p><%= app.domain %> · <%= app.status %></p><% if app.status == 'failed' && (@access.directory_admin? || LightekIdentity::Permissions.ids(current_user,'GatekeeperHostedApplication','manage').include?(app.id)) %><%= button_to 'Retry existing application setup', dashboard_directory_retry_application_path(app,employer_id: @employer.id), class: 'lp-button secondary' %><% end %></article><% end %></div></section>
<% if @access.directory_admin? %><section class="lp-card"><h2>Company MFA policy</h2><p>Corporate workspaces start with MFA required for the owner and active members. Enrollment-only sign-in cannot open business features. Financial access and privileged platform staff keep mandatory MFA even if this company-wide setting is relaxed.</p><%= form_with url: dashboard_directory_policy_path(employer_id: @employer.id),class: 'lp-form' do |f| %><label class="lp-check"><%= check_box_tag :mfa_required,'1',@organization_policy.nil? || @organization_policy.mfa_required? %> Require MFA for everyone in this employer</label><label>Current password<%= f.password_field :password,required: true,autocomplete: 'current-password' %></label><%= f.submit 'Save company policy',class: 'lp-button secondary' %><% end %></section><section class="lp-card"><h2>IT directory administration</h2><p>The employer owner explicitly appoints IT administrators under People &amp; access. IT manages directory identities, security-bearing department assignments, SSO, domain joining and resource grants. This permission does not grant HR, payroll or accounting access.</p><% @members.each do |member| %><details><summary><%= member.worker.full_name %> · <%= member.title %></summary><%= form_with scope: :membership,url: dashboard_directory_member_path(member,employer_id: @employer.id),class: 'lp-form' do |f| %><label>Directory login principal<%= f.text_field :directory_principal,value: member.directory_principal,placeholder: 'person@ad.company.com' %></label><label>Department<%= f.select :department_id,@departments.map { |d| [d.name,d.id] },{include_blank: 'Unassigned',selected: member.department_id} %></label><label>Current password<%= password_field_tag :password,nil,required: true,autocomplete: 'current-password' %></label><%= f.submit 'Save directory membership',class: 'lp-button secondary' %><% end %></details><% end %></section><section class="lp-card"><h2>Resource permissions</h2><p>Changes require your current password and a verified authenticator session. Department grants apply to direct members of that department. Application permissions do not grant a client-owner management session or new provisioning spend.</p><%= form_with url: dashboard_directory_grants_path(employer_id: @employer.id), class: 'lp-form' do |f| %><div class="lp-grid"><label>Person or department<%= f.select :subject_key, @members.map { |m| ["#{m.worker.full_name} · #{m.title}","employment:#{m.id}"] } + @departments.map { |d| ["Department · #{d.name}","department:#{d.id}"] }, {}, required: true %></label><label>Server or application<%= f.select :resource_key, @nodes.map { |n| ["Server · #{n.name}","server:#{n.id}"] } + @applications.map { |a| ["Application · #{a.name}","application:#{a.id}"] }, {}, required: true %></label><label>Permission<%= f.select :permission, [['Read','read'],['Manage existing resource','manage'],['Domain login (server only)','login']] %></label><label>Current password<%= f.password_field :password, required: true, autocomplete: 'current-password' %></label></div><%= f.submit 'Grant permission', class: 'lp-button' %><% end %><% @grants.each do |grant| %><article class="lp-election"><div><strong><%= grant.subject.respond_to?(:worker) ? grant.subject.worker.full_name : grant.subject.name %></strong><p><%= grant.permission.humanize %> · <%= grant.resource.name %></p></div><%= form_with url: dashboard_directory_grant_path(grant,employer_id: @employer.id), method: :delete, class: 'lp-form' do |f| %><%= f.password_field :password, required: true, placeholder: 'Current password', aria: {label: 'Current password to revoke permission'} %><%= f.submit 'Revoke permission', class: 'lp-button secondary' %><% end %></article><% end %></section>
<section class="lp-card"><h2>Organization sign-in</h2><p>Use an OIDC provider such as Entra ID or Keycloak. Configure its exact issuer and public HTTPS endpoints, then register <code><%= identity_sso_callback_url %></code> as the callback. Local sign-in remains available.</p><%= form_with scope: :connection, url: dashboard_directory_connection_path(employer_id: @employer.id), class: 'lp-form' do |f| %><% %w[slug issuer authorization_endpoint token_endpoint jwks_uri client_id].each do |key| %><label><%= key == 'slug' ? 'Organization code' : key.humanize %><%= f.text_field key, value: @connection&.public_send(key), required: true %></label><% end %><label>Client secret · leave blank to keep current<%= f.password_field :client_secret, autocomplete: 'new-password' %></label><label class="lp-check"><%= f.check_box :enabled, checked: @connection.nil? || @connection.enabled? %> Enable organization sign-in</label><label>Current Lightek password<%= password_field_tag :password, nil, required: true, autocomplete: 'current-password' %></label><%= f.submit 'Save SSO connection in Vault', class: 'lp-button' %><% end %></section>
<section class="lp-card"><h2>Domain joining</h2><p>Join remote Ubuntu servers to an existing Active Directory or Samba AD domain. The server must already use that domain’s DNS and have network/time synchronization. Lightek manages the permitted domain principals; existing local administrator access remains available. It does not create a new domain controller.</p><%= form_with scope: :realm, url: dashboard_directory_realm_path(employer_id: @employer.id), class: 'lp-form' do |f| %><label>Domain<%= f.text_field :domain, value: @realm&.domain, required: true, placeholder: 'ad.company.com' %></label><label>Delegated domain join user<%= f.text_field :join_user, autocomplete: 'off' %></label><label>Join password · leave blank to keep current<%= f.password_field :join_password, autocomplete: 'new-password' %></label><label class="lp-check"><%= f.check_box :enabled, checked: @realm.nil? || @realm.enabled? %> Enable directory logins</label><label class="lp-check"><%= f.check_box :auto_join, checked: @realm&.auto_join? %> Automatically join healthy remote servers owned by this employer</label><label>Current Lightek password<%= password_field_tag :password, nil, required: true, autocomplete: 'current-password' %></label><%= f.submit 'Save domain settings in Vault', class: 'lp-button' %><% end %><% @nodes.reject(&:local?).each do |node| %><article class="lp-election"><div><strong><%= node.name %></strong><p><% binding = @bindings.detect { |b| b.gatekeeper_node_id == node.id } %><%= binding&.status || 'Not joined' %> · <%= binding&.synced_at %> <%= binding&.error_code %></p></div><%= form_with url: dashboard_directory_join_path(node,employer_id: @employer.id), class: 'lp-form' do |f| %><%= f.password_field :password, required: true, placeholder: 'Current password', aria: {label: 'Current password to join or sync this server'} %><%= f.submit 'Join / reconcile allowlist', class: 'lp-button secondary' %><% end %></article><% end %></section><% end %></main>
